{%- comment -%}
  Group Buy campaign page (README "Live Savings / Progress" +
  "Group Buy Options / Cart" +
  docs/SLICE-2-AND-GROUP-BUY-OWNER-DECISIONS.md §9-§12).

  STATUS: all customer-facing copy this file introduces is DRAFT, pending
  owner approval, EXCEPT `templates.group_buy_campaign.sign_in_required_message`,
  which is the byte-for-byte owner-approved sentence from
  docs/REQUIRED-CUSTOMER-ACCOUNTS.md §4 and is pinned in
  app/app/theme/ownerApprovedCopy.test.ts alongside its twins in
  snippets/bank-payment-checkout-dialog.liquid and
  sections/warranty-claim-form.liquid. Do not reword that one sentence
  without owner sign-off; every other string here is a reasonable first
  draft, shipped functional per the architect's standing instruction rather
  than blocked on approval (same precedent as the two files above).

  WHAT THIS FILE CONSUMES, AND DOES NOT DUPLICATE. Every price, tier, unit
  count, savings figure and countdown comes from the existing read-only
  App Proxy endpoint (`GET /apps/carat/group-buy/:code`,
  app/app/routes/apps.carat.group-buy.$code.tsx). Nothing about tiers,
  rounding or the Bank/Card rule is computed here — a template that did its
  own arithmetic would be a second place a customer-facing price is decided,
  and the two could disagree. This section calls that SAME endpoint once per
  distinct Shopify variant it needs a price for (the endpoint's own
  docstring names exactly this caller: "a theme knows Shopify variant ids").

  ONLY ONE ACTIVE PRICE AT A TIME (owner §9/§10). The public/default price is
  the Regular/Card Price. A required Payment Type selection (unchecked by
  default — CLAUDE.md: a required choice is never pre-checked) switches the
  SAME slot to the Bank Payment Price; the two are never shown side by side.
  This reproduces the pattern already reviewed and shipped in
  `app/extensions/group-buy-progress` (a product-page app block covering the
  live-savings figures) — that block is out of scope for this task (nothing
  under `app/` besides tests) and does not offer a configuration table or an
  ordering flow, which is what this dedicated campaign PAGE adds.

  THE COMPARISON TABLE IS NATIVE-SHOPIFY-FIRST, NOT JSON-FIRST. Rows come
  straight from the bound product's own `variants`/`options_with_values` —
  real Shopify data, so a row can never claim a configuration Shopify itself
  does not sell. The versioned campaign-options JSON contract
  (`app/app/domain/groupbuy/campaignOptions.ts`, deferred formal tooling
  until Slice 6) has no variant-id field and cannot resolve a combination to
  a specific price on its own — it describes WHAT MAY BE SOLD, not which
  Shopify variant that is. So this file uses the JSON for exactly what it
  can honestly provide before that tooling exists: which of the product's
  OWN option names appear as table columns, and in what order
  (`tableView.columns`, matched case-insensitively against
  `product.options_with_values`). Absent JSON, or JSON that matches nothing,
  the table simply shows every native product option — the page still works
  for a merchant who has not yet authored the JSON. See
  `campaign_options_json` in the schema below.

  ACCOUNT REQUIRED (docs/REQUIRED-CUSTOMER-ACCOUNTS.md). Browsing signed out
  is fine — the table, the live progress figures and the Payment Type price
  toggle all render for every visitor. Only the ORDER ACTION itself (the
  `{%- if customer -%}` branch below, around "Order this configuration") is
  gated: a signed-out visitor sees the pinned sign-in sentence and a sign-in
  link in that spot instead of a working control. This is a server-side
  render-time branch on Liquid's own `customer` object — the same pattern
  proven in `snippets/bank-payment-checkout-dialog.liquid` and
  `sections/warranty-claim-form.liquid` — not a client-side hide-after-render,
  and it is UX, not enforcement: nothing under `app/` is touched by this
  task, and any future Group Buy order-creation route must independently
  reject an unauthenticated request.

  TWO ORDERING PATHS, TWO MECHANISMS — BOTH REAL NOW.

  The Credit/Debit Card path uses Shopify's own native `/cart/add`: the bound
  product/variant is an ordinary Shopify product and native cart/checkout is
  the correct default per CLAUDE.md's "prefer Shopify-native capabilities"
  principle.

  The Bank Payment path cannot use it. Native checkout cannot vary the
  payable total by payment method (`docs/BANK-PAYMENT-CHECKOUT-FINDINGS.md`),
  so a customer choosing Bank Payment had no way to be charged the Bank
  Payment Price. This file therefore used to show a plain "Contact us to
  arrange payment" link — honest at the time, because no Group Buy Bank
  Payment endpoint existed to call.

  THAT IS NO LONGER TRUE, AND THE LINK IS GONE (register D12).
  `POST /apps/carat/group-buy-bank-checkout` creates a server-priced, real,
  unpaid Shopify order at the frozen campaign tier, and
  `snippets/group-buy-bank-payment-form.liquid` calls it. Read that snippet's
  header before touching the acknowledgment handling: the Card and Bank
  acknowledgment MECHANISMS are deliberately different (the Card path must
  carry an id into native checkout; the Bank path must not accept one from
  the browser), while the EVIDENCE STANDARD is identical and pinned by
  `groupBuyAcknowledgmentEvidenceParity.test.ts`.

  THIS SECTION DOES NOT USE `<product-form>`/`assets/product-form.js`. That
  component's second submit button switches the CART-WIDE Buy Now Bank
  Payment Discount mode (owner §20) — a different feature with its own
  eligibility flag, 24-hour lock and 2%-autopublish rules. Reusing it here
  would conflate Buy Now Bank Payment pricing with Group Buy's frozen tier
  pricing and risk exactly what CLAUDE.md rule 21 forbids: Buy Now and Group
  Buy sharing one cart/order. This section's own tiny form only ever posts a
  plain native `/cart/add` for the Card path.
{%- endcomment -%}
{{ 'component-group-buy-campaign.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

{%- style -%}
  .section-{{ section.id }}-padding {
    padding-top: {{ section.settings.padding_top | times: 0.75 | round: 0 }}px;
    padding-bottom: {{ section.settings.padding_bottom | times: 0.75 | round: 0 }}px;
  }

  @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
    .section-{{ section.id }}-padding {
      padding-top: {{ section.settings.padding_top }}px;
      padding-bottom: {{ section.settings.padding_bottom }}px;
    }
  }
{%- endstyle -%}

{%- liquid
  assign campaign_code = section.settings.campaign_code | strip
  assign gb_product = section.settings.product
  assign campaign_options_raw = section.settings.campaign_options_json | strip
-%}

<div class="color-{{ section.settings.color_scheme }} gradient">
  {%- comment -%}
    `page-width`, not `page-width--narrow`. The functional header above and
    the how-it-works steps below both sit at the page-width edge, so a
    narrower container here put the campaign — and the empty state — on a
    second, unexplained left margin partway down the page.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="page-width section-{{ section.id }}-padding carat-gb-campaign">
    {%- if campaign_code == blank or gb_product == blank -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        Merchant-only placeholder. Never rendered to a real shopper: without
        both settings there is no campaign to call and no product to sell,
        so showing nothing (outside the theme editor) is safer than a
        broken widget.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if request.design_mode -%}
        <p class="carat-gb-campaign__onboarding">
          {{- 'templates.group_buy_campaign.onboarding_missing_settings' | t -}}
        </p>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- comment -%}
        SHOPPER-VISIBLE EMPTY STATE (owner decision 2026-10-30).

        Rendering nothing is the right answer to a MISCONFIGURED campaign —
        that is what the comment above protects against, and it still holds.
        But it was also the answer when no campaign happened to be running,
        which left a customer who clicked "Group Buy" on a page that
        explained the idea and offered no way to act on it, with no word of
        why. Silence read as broken.

        So: still nothing clever, still no half-built widget. Just a plain
        statement of the situation and the three routes that do work today.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="carat-gb-empty">
        <h2 class="carat-gb-empty__title">No Group Buy is open right now</h2>
        <p class="carat-gb-empty__text">
          Campaigns open for a set window. When the next one opens it will appear here &mdash;
          and in the meantime there are other ways to buy.
        </p>
        <div class="carat-gb-empty__actions">
          <a class="button" href="{{ routes.root_url }}pages/past-group-buys">See past Group Buys</a>
          <a class="button button--secondary" href="{{ routes.root_url }}pages/custom-jewelry">Design something custom</a>
          <a class="button button--secondary" href="{{ routes.root_url }}pages/luxury-steals">Luxury Steals</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    {%- else -%}
      <div
        class="carat-gb-campaign__root"
        data-carat-gb-campaign
        data-campaign-code="{{ campaign_code | escape }}"
        data-money-format="{{ shop.money_format | escape }}"
        data-cart-add-url="{{ routes.cart_add_url }}"
        data-cart-url="{{ routes.cart_url }}"
        {%- if campaign_options_raw != blank -%}
          data-campaign-options="{{ campaign_options_raw | escape }}"
        {%- endif -%}
      >
        {%- comment -%}
          `sections/main-page.liquid` (rendered first in
          templates/page.group-buy.json) already shows the Shopify PAGE's own
          title as an <h1> — same convention as
          `sections/warranty-claim-form.liquid` and `contact-form.liquid`. So
          this is always an <h2>: either the merchant's override, or the
          bound product's own title, which is genuinely useful supplementary
          context (a page titled "Summer Group Buy" selling a "Solitaire Ring")
          rather than a duplicate page heading.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if section.settings.heading != blank -%}
          <h2 class="title title-wrapper--no-top-margin {{ section.settings.heading_size }}">
            {{ section.settings.heading }}
          </h2>
        {%- else -%}
          <h2 class="title title-wrapper--no-top-margin {{ section.settings.heading_size }}">
            {{ gb_product.title | escape }}
          </h2>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if section.settings.subheading != blank -%}
          <div class="carat-gb-campaign__subheading rte">{{ section.settings.subheading }}</div>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- comment -%}
          Lightweight Share/Copy Link (README "Group Buy Sharing"). Hand-rolled
          rather than `{% render 'share-button' %}` because that snippet reads
          `block.settings.share_label`/`block.shopify_attributes` from a real
          section BLOCK, which this section does not have — the markup below
          is otherwise identical to `snippets/share-button.liquid` so the
          existing `<share-button>` custom element (assets/share.js) drives it
          unchanged.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <script src="{{ 'share.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>
        <share-button id="Share-{{ section.id }}" class="share-button carat-gb-campaign__share">
          <button class="share-button__button hidden">
            <span class="svg-wrapper">{{ 'icon-share.svg' | inline_asset_content }}</span>
            {{ 'templates.group_buy_campaign.share_label' | t }}
          </button>
          <details id="Details-{{ section.id }}-share">
            <summary class="share-button__button">
              <span class="svg-wrapper">{{ 'icon-share.svg' | inline_asset_content }}</span>
              {{ 'templates.group_buy_campaign.share_label' | t }}
            </summary>
            <div class="share-button__fallback motion-reduce">
              <div class="field">
                <span id="ShareMessage-{{ section.id }}" class="share-button__message hidden" role="status"> </span>
                <input
                  type="text"
                  class="field__input"
                  id="ShareUrl-{{ section.id }}"
                  value="{{ canonical_url }}"
                  placeholder="{{ 'general.share.share_url' | t }}"
                  onclick="this.select();"
                  readonly
                >
                <label class="field__label" for="ShareUrl-{{ section.id }}">{{ 'general.share.share_url' | t }}</label>
              </div>
              <button class="share-button__close hidden">
                <span class="svg-wrapper">{{- 'icon-close.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}</span>
                <span class="visually-hidden">{{ 'general.share.close' | t }}</span>
              </button>
              <button class="share-button__copy">
                <span class="svg-wrapper">{{- 'icon-copy.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}</span>
                <span class="visually-hidden">{{ 'general.share.copy_to_clipboard' | t }}</span>
              </button>
            </div>
          </details>
        </share-button>

        {%- comment -%}
          Native Shopify product/variant data, read once, server-rendered —
          the source of truth for "what may be sold" and "is it in stock".
          JS never re-derives this from anything else.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <script type="application/json" data-carat-gb-variants>
          {{ gb_product.variants | json }}
        </script>
        <script type="application/json" data-carat-gb-options>
          {{ gb_product.options_with_values | json }}
        </script>

        {%- comment -%}
          LOADING / UNAVAILABLE, aria-live so a screen-reader hears the
          figures when they arrive — same treatment as
          `group-buy-progress.js`'s own block, and for the same reason: this
          fills in without a page load, which is otherwise silent.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <p class="carat-gb-campaign__loading" data-carat-gb-campaign-loading>
          {{ 'templates.group_buy_campaign.loading' | t }}
        </p>
        <noscript>
          <p class="carat-gb-campaign__unavailable">{{ 'templates.group_buy_campaign.noscript' | t }}</p>
        </noscript>

        <div
          class="carat-gb-campaign__body"
          data-carat-gb-campaign-body
          aria-live="polite"
          aria-busy="true"
          hidden
        >
          {%- comment -%}
            README "Group Buy Options / Cart": the public comparison table.
            Regular/Card Price ONLY (owner §10) — never a second price
            column — with the required note directly beneath it. JS fills
            <thead>/<tbody>; the two are empty here on purpose (§10: "renders
            nothing until it has real data" — the same discipline as
            group-buy-progress.js).
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <div class="carat-gb-campaign__table-wrap">
            <h2 class="carat-gb-campaign__section-heading">
              {{ 'templates.group_buy_campaign.table_heading' | t }}
            </h2>
            <table class="carat-gb-campaign__table" data-carat-gb-table>
              <thead data-carat-gb-table-head></thead>
              <tbody data-carat-gb-table-body></tbody>
            </table>
            <p class="carat-gb-campaign__bank-note">
              {{ 'templates.group_buy_campaign.bank_note' | t }}
            </p>
          </div>

          {%- comment -%}
            Configuration + required Payment Type + the single active price
            slot (owner §9). Native <select> per product option — real
            semantic form controls, populated server-side, so the page works
            before this section's own JS finishes loading; the JS only
            attaches `change` listeners and resolves the matching variant.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <div class="carat-gb-campaign__configurator" data-carat-gb-configurator>
            <h2 class="carat-gb-campaign__section-heading">
              {{ 'templates.group_buy_campaign.configure_heading' | t }}
            </h2>
            <div class="carat-gb-campaign__options" data-carat-gb-option-selects>
              {%- for option in gb_product.options_with_values -%}
                <div class="carat-gb-campaign__option field">
                  <label class="field__label" for="CaratGbOption-{{ section.id }}-{{ forloop.index0 }}">
                    {{ option.name }}
                  </label>
                  <div class="select">
                    <select
                      id="CaratGbOption-{{ section.id }}-{{ forloop.index0 }}"
                      class="select__select"
                      data-carat-gb-option-index="{{ forloop.index0 }}"
                    >
                      {%- for value in option.values -%}
                        <option value="{{ value | escape }}">{{ value }}</option>
                      {%- endfor -%}
                    </select>
                    <span class="svg-wrapper">{{- 'icon-caret.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}</span>
                  </div>
                </div>
              {%- endfor -%}
            </div>

            <p class="carat-gb-campaign__variant-status" role="status" data-carat-gb-variant-status hidden></p>

            {%- comment -%}
              Required Payment Type (owner §9/§10) — NEITHER radio checked by
              default. CLAUDE.md: a required acknowledgment/choice is never
              pre-checked or silently inferred.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <fieldset class="carat-gb-campaign__payment-type">
              <legend class="carat-gb-campaign__payment-type-legend">
                {{ 'templates.group_buy_campaign.payment_type_legend' | t }}
              </legend>
              <label class="carat-gb-campaign__payment-option">
                <input
                  type="radio"
                  name="carat-gb-payment-type-{{ section.id }}"
                  value="card"
                  data-carat-gb-payment-type
                >
                {{ 'templates.group_buy_campaign.payment_type_card' | t }}
              </label>
              <label class="carat-gb-campaign__payment-option">
                <input
                  type="radio"
                  name="carat-gb-payment-type-{{ section.id }}"
                  value="bank"
                  data-carat-gb-payment-type
                >
                {{ 'templates.group_buy_campaign.payment_type_bank' | t }}
              </label>
            </fieldset>

            <div class="carat-gb-campaign__price-active" data-carat-gb-active-price></div>
          </div>

          {%- comment -%}
            ORDER ACTION — gated on sign-in (docs/REQUIRED-CUSTOMER-ACCOUNTS.md
            §4). See this file's header comment for why the two actions below
            are shaped the way they are.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- if customer -%}
            <div class="carat-gb-campaign__order" data-carat-gb-order>
              <h2 class="carat-gb-campaign__section-heading">
                {{ 'templates.group_buy_campaign.order_heading' | t }}
              </h2>
              <p class="carat-gb-campaign__order-hint" data-carat-gb-order-hint>
                {{ 'templates.group_buy_campaign.order_hint' | t }}
              </p>

              {%- comment -%}
                Group Buy cancellation-policy acknowledgment (owner spec
                2026-09-27/28). CAPTURE + UX GATE ONLY, NOT ENFORCEMENT — the
                binding control is the `orders/create` order-time
                verification in `groupBuyOrderHandler.server.ts`; this
                checkbox can only stop a customer who actually uses this page,
                never a direct `/cart/add` POST. Required before EITHER
                action below (see `canSubmitOrder` in group-buy-campaign.js),
                never pre-checked. `required` on the checkbox itself is a
                progressive-enhancement backstop for a JS-disabled visitor —
                same reasoning as `luxury-product-gate.liquid`'s identical
                attribute on its own checkbox.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              <div class="carat-gb-campaign__cancellation-ack" data-carat-gb-cancel-ack>
                <p class="carat-gb-campaign__cancellation-disclosure" id="CaratGbCancelDisclosure-{{ section.id }}">
                  {{- 'templates.group_buy_campaign.cancellation_disclosure' | t -}}
                </p>
                <label class="carat-gb-campaign__cancellation-checkbox-row">
                  <input
                    type="checkbox"
                    id="CaratGbCancelCheckbox-{{ section.id }}"
                    data-carat-gb-cancel-ack-checkbox
                    aria-describedby="CaratGbCancelDisclosure-{{ section.id }}"
                    required
                  >
                  <span class="visually-hidden">{{ 'templates.group_buy_campaign.cancellation_checkbox_label' | t }}: </span>
                  {{- 'templates.group_buy_campaign.cancellation_affirm_label' | t -}}
                </label>
                <p
                  class="carat-gb-campaign__cancellation-status"
                  role="status"
                  data-carat-gb-cancel-ack-status
                  hidden
                ></p>
                <p class="carat-gb-campaign__cancellation-error" role="alert" data-carat-gb-cancel-ack-error hidden>
                  {{- 'templates.group_buy_campaign.cancellation_ack_error' | t -}}
                </p>
                <input
                  type="hidden"
                  name="properties[_carat_gb_cancel_ack]"
                  value=""
                  data-carat-gb-cancel-ack-input
                >
              </div>

              <form data-carat-gb-add-to-cart-form>
                <input type="hidden" name="id" value="" data-carat-gb-variant-id>
                <input type="hidden" name="quantity" value="1">
                <button
                  type="submit"
                  class="button button--full-width"
                  data-carat-gb-add-to-cart
                  data-carat-gb-payment-type-target="card"
                  disabled
                >
                  <span>{{ 'templates.group_buy_campaign.add_to_cart' | t }}</span>
                  {%- render 'loading-spinner' -%}
                </button>
              </form>

              {%- comment -%}
                BANK PAYMENT — a real ordering path as of register D12.
                This was a "Contact us to arrange payment" link for as long
                as no Group Buy Bank Payment endpoint existed. One exists now
                (`POST /apps/carat/group-buy-bank-checkout`) and this form
                calls it. See the snippet's own header for why its
                acknowledgment mechanism is deliberately NOT the Card path's.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              {%- render 'group-buy-bank-payment-form', section: section -%}

              {%- comment -%}
                The confirmation replaces the form on success. Built by JS
                from the server-composed instructions object — never by
                Liquid, because it carries bank coordinates.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              <div class="carat-gb-bank-confirmation" data-carat-gb-bank-confirmation hidden></div>
            </div>
          {%- else -%}
            <div class="carat-gb-campaign__signin-required" data-carat-gb-signin-required>
              <h3 class="carat-gb-campaign__signin-heading">
                {{- 'templates.group_buy_campaign.sign_in_required_heading' | t -}}
              </h3>
              <p class="carat-gb-campaign__signin-message">
                {{- 'templates.group_buy_campaign.sign_in_required_message' | t -}}
              </p>
              <a
                href="{{ routes.account_login_url }}?return_url={{ request.path | url_encode }}"
                class="button"
                data-carat-gb-signin-link
              >
                {{- 'customer.log_in' | t -}}
              </a>
            </div>
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- comment -%}
            README "Live Savings / Progress" — tier track, countdown, Best
            Price Unlocked, core message. A track of THRESHOLDS, never a
            crowdfunding-style "% funded" figure — the README forbids the
            latter outright, and JS never builds one.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <div class="carat-gb-campaign__progress" data-carat-gb-progress></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</div>

<script src="{{ 'group-buy-campaign.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Group Buy campaign",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "section",
  "disabled_on": {
    "groups": ["header", "footer"]
  },
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "product",
      "id": "product",
      "label": "Campaign product"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "campaign_code",
      "label": "Campaign code",
      "info": "The Group Buy campaign code from the CaratForUs admin."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "heading",
      "label": "Heading",
      "info": "Defaults to the product title when left blank."
    },
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "subheading",
      "label": "Subheading"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "heading_size",
      "options": [
        { "value": "h2", "label": "Small" },
        { "value": "h1", "label": "Medium" },
        { "value": "h0", "label": "Large" }
      ],
      "default": "h1",
      "label": "Heading size"
    },
    {
      "type": "color_scheme",
      "id": "color_scheme",
      "label": "Color scheme",
      "default": "scheme-1"
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "campaign_options_json",
      "label": "Campaign options JSON (advanced)",
      "info": "Optional. The versioned Group Buy campaign-options JSON (schemaVersion, optionDimensions, tableView, orderingFlow — see app/app/domain/groupbuy/campaignOptions.ts). Used only to choose which of the product's own options appear as table columns and in what order. Leave blank to show every product option."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Section padding"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_top",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "label": "Top padding",
      "default": 36
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_bottom",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "label": "Bottom padding",
      "default": 36
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Group Buy campaign"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
